\title{FRI}
\author{dhsorens}
\date{2026-08-18}

\p{
    Fast Reed–Solomon Interactive Oracle Proof of Proximity. The protocol most of the deployed
    proving stack rests on, and the one every construction later in this section is a response to.
}

\p{
    Questions this page should answer:
    \ul{
        \li{The folding map: halving the degree by splitting into even and odd parts and taking a
        random combination. Why the folded word is a codeword when the original is.}
        \li{Commit phase and query phase; the round-consistency check the verifier performs.}
        \li{Parameters and their interaction: rate, folding factor, number of rounds, number of
        query repetitions.}
        \li{Prover cost — encoding, Merkle hashing, and where the time actually goes.}
        \li{[The soundness statement](dhsorens-004L), with the [regime](dhsorens-0038) named
        explicitly.}
        \li{What ArkLib's \code{ProofSystem/Fri} states, and how far the proof gets.}
    }
}

\p{
    Reading: Ben-Sasson, Bentov, Horesh, and Riabzev, \em{Fast Reed–Solomon Interactive Oracle
    Proofs of Proximity} (ICALP 2018); [the SoK](https://eprint.iacr.org/2026/1367) for the
    corrected attributions.
}
